SPDX-License-Identifier: LGPL-2.1-only WITH OCCT-exception-1.0

Offset: the enlarged face of a spindle torus stops at its apexes, and an
offset whose unwinding keeps no shell is an error, not success with no
shape (mitcad#2457, GitHub mitcad/Mitcad#678).

1. A shelled block with rounded edges, a rounded bead along its outline
   that ends at a corner in a spindle torus (major radius 0.6, minor 1.4:
   it meets itself at two apexes on its axis), some faces moved by their
   own offsets and every other face at 0 (MitCad's Offset Face): the
   offset gave no shape, whatever faces it moved, also faces far from the
   corner. EnLargeFace enlarges a face on a periodic surface by a tenth of
   the rest of the period on each side; the torus face (v from 3pi/2 to
   2pi) was enlarged past the apex (at v = -acos(-R/r), 0.03 rad beyond its
   reach), into the torus' other part. There the face's offset met its
   neighbours' a second time (a loop of the intersection round the apex),
   its own loop did not close, the outer rounding beside it was left as its
   untrimmed enlarged face, and the unwinding of the shells dropped the
   shell with those free edges. The enlarged face of a spindle torus, also
   given as an offset surface of a torus, now stops at the apexes on the
   face's side, as a cone's stops at its apex, and MakeFace takes the iso
   at an apex for a point (a degenerated edge), as it does a cone's.

2. Where the unwinding (SelectShells) keeps no shell, MakeOffsetShape
   reported success with no shape (IsDone true, no error): MitCad read the
   empty result ("the offset produced no solid"), and in 0.72.0 on Windows
   the Offset Face of the reported design ended in an access violation.
   It is now not done, with BRepOffset_UnknownError.

On the reported body the offset now closes (the four faces moved 2 mm, the
sum of the four moves). On the chain without patch 2418 one edge of it comes
out with a tolerance of 2.9 mm: the tangent edge between two faces that keep
their offset 0 (a sloped plane and a swept band, a B-spline whose parameter
runs 38 times faster than the edge's), trimmed where the moved faces' new
positions meet them; BRepOffset_Inter2d's ExtendPCurve makes the band's
straight curve under the edge (a two-pole B-spline over [-2.72, 0]) a line
of unit speed from its first pole. With patch 2418 before this one, as in
MitCad's port, the result is valid (23801.198 mm3 in MitCad).

The patch's test and its before/after proof:
third_party/vcpkg-ports/docs/opencascade-patch-tests.md, section 2457.

